**[named bool] bare true/false passed as an argument**

The bare true binds to the parameter kv of the local lambda add [t/t_llama_unit.cpp:3768]: whether the job has KV work. One pair next to the lambda serves lines 3781, 3785, 3789, 3792 and 3794.

Proposed:
```cpp
// next to the add lambda:
constexpr bool KV_TRUE = true;  // add(tok, kv): the job has KV work
constexpr bool KV_FALSE = false;

    add(tok, KV_TRUE);
```

**[named bool] bare true/false passed as an argument**

The bare false binds to the parameter converted of the local lambda check_blocks [t/t_llama_unit.cpp:3912]. The /*converted=*/ comment carries the meaning, but the literal is still bare under the rule. page::CONVERTED_TRUE and CONVERTED_FALSE in kv_cache.hpp sit after `private:` [h/tron/models/kv_cache.hpp:2479], so the test needs its own pair; one pair serves lines 3934, 3936, 3956, 3958, 3976, 3978, 4004 and 4006.

Proposed:
```cpp
// next to the check_blocks lambda:
constexpr bool CONVERTED_FALSE = false;  // check_blocks(converted)
constexpr bool CONVERTED_TRUE = true;

    check_blocks(CONVERTED_FALSE);
```
